<title>UK: DuPont to hike titanium dioxide price - paper.</title>
<headline>DuPont to hike titanium dioxide price - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>DuPont, the world's largest producer of titanium dioxide, is to raise its prices in an effort to lift the huge commodity industry out of the doldrums, the Financial Times (FT) newsaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>DuPont, which holds 25 percent of the world titanium dioxide market, plans to increase its U.S. prices by 4.5 percent on January 1 and European prices by between five and eight percent, the FT said.</p>
<p>Titanium dioxide, with global sales of more than $7 billion a year, is the main ingredient in paint and paper coatings. It is also used to colour plastics.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
